   $q$In $\triangle ABC$, $D$ is on $\overline{AB}$ and $E$ is on $\overline{AC}$ with $\overline{DE} \parallel \overline{BC}$. If $AD = x$, $DB = 6$, $AE = 8$ and $EC = 12$, what is $x$?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$x = 4$","is_correct":true},{"text":"$x = 16$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"mismatched-segments"},{"text":"$x = 2$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"subtracted-instead-of-dividing"},{"text":"$x = 9$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"inverted-proportion"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$x = 4$$q$, $q$By the triangle proportionality theorem, $\frac{x}{6} = \frac{8}{12}$, so $x = 6 \cdot \frac{2}{3} = 4$. The choice 9 comes from $\frac{x}{6} = \frac{12}{8}$, which flips one of the ratios.$q$, 'draft', null)
