   $q$To measure across a pond, Tomasz marks points so that $\triangle ABC$ and $\triangle ADE$ share vertex $A$, with $B$ on $\overline{AD}$, $C$ on $\overline{AE}$, and $\overline{BC} \parallel \overline{DE}$. He measures $AB = 30$ m, $BC = 18$ m and $AD = 50$ m. How long is $\overline{DE}$?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$38$ m","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"added-difference"},{"text":"$10.8$ m","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"inverted-ratio"},{"text":"$45$ m","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"used-segment-not-whole-side"},{"text":"$30$ m","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$30$ m$q$, $q$Since $\overline{BC} \parallel \overline{DE}$, $\triangle ABC \sim \triangle ADE$ by AA, so $\frac{DE}{18} = \frac{50}{30}$ and $DE = 30$ m. The choice 45 m uses $BD = 20$ in place of $AB = 30$, but the matching side of $\triangle ABC$ is the whole side $AB$.$q$, 'draft', null)
