   $q$Points $A$, $C$, $E$ are collinear and points $B$, $C$, $D$ are collinear, so $\overline{AE}$ and $\overline{BD}$ cross at $C$. Also $\overline{AB} \parallel \overline{DE}$. Which similarity statement is correct?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$\\triangle ABC \\sim \\triangle CDE$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"listed-vertices-alphabetically"},{"text":"$\\triangle ABC \\sim \\triangle DCE$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignored-alternate-angles"},{"text":"$\\triangle ABC \\sim \\triangle DEC$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"swapped-corresponding-vertices"},{"text":"$\\triangle ABC \\sim \\triangle EDC$","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$\triangle ABC \sim \triangle EDC$$q$, $q$With $\overline{AB} \parallel \overline{DE}$, alternate interior angles give $\angle A \cong \angle E$ and $\angle B \cong \angle D$, and the vertical angles at $C$ match, so $A \to E$, $B \to D$, $C \to C$ and $\triangle ABC \sim \triangle EDC$. The choice $\triangle DEC$ pairs $A$ with $D$, but $\angle A$ is actually equal to $\angle E$.$q$, 'draft', null)
